  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Jass (Schieber). Logic: See rules.objective and rules.gameplay.',
    Player: "Jass is the national card game of Switzerland, specifically the 'Schieber' variant, which is a four-player partnership trick-taking game. It features a unique 36-card deck (Acorns, Bells, Shields, Flowers) and a complex point-tracking system. The game is highly strategic, requiring players to deduce their partner's strength through 'pushing' the trump selection and careful card signaling.",
    objective: 'Score a target number of points (usually 1000 or 2500) through trick-taking and melds (Weis).',
    gameplay: '1. Must follow suit. If unable, you can trump or discard.\n2. **StÃ¶ck**: Holding the King and Ober of the trump suit (20 pts).\n3. **Weis**: Melds declared during the first trick (e.g., four of a kind, sequences).',
    keyRules: [
      'Must follow suit if possible; may trump or discard if unable. When trumping, must overtrump if holding a higher trump.',
      'Puur (trump Jack) need not be played when it is the only trump in hand.',
      'Eldest (right of dealer) leads to the first trick; winner of each trick leads next.',
      'Stöck (King and Ober of trumps) scores 20 when claimed on playing the second card to a trick.',
      'Weis (melds) are declared when contributing to the first trick; only the best meld scores.',
    ],
